      "Feasibility and Development Plan": "• High – the project has demonstrable milestones (cell isolation, prototypes) and a detailed roadmap for pilot testing and production scaling. Patent-pending scaffolding is a strong indicator of technical progress.",
      "Revenue Model and Sustainability": "• Moderate – reliant on jewelry sales. The unique material and ethical sourcing could command a premium price, but scaling production presents challenges.",
      "Differentiation": "• High – the cultivated leather itself is a truly unique and differentiated product. The animal welfare aspect adds another layer of appeal.",
      "Impact and Evidence Plan": "• Low – The impact is primarily ethical (animal welfare).  There’s no evidence presented to support the quality or durability of the cultivated leather or the long-term viability of the process.",
      "Risk Awareness and Mitigation": "• Moderate – identifies several risks (cell loss, texture variability, supply chain), but the mitigation strategies (pilot testing, inspection) are reasonable.  Dependency on specific settings is a concern."
    }
  },
  "winner": "B"
}
